6349:The first symbolic claim closed with `#Top`, confirming that the full translated function—not a hand-written shortcut—proves for arbitrary two-element float inputs. I’m now simplifying the pair enumeration from nested loops to one index-state loop. It is behaviorally identical, but it permits a single universal loop invariant that K can prove by circularity and then reuse as a separately proved lemma for the entry-point theorem.
